# Gadget Galaxy - HTML Project

##  Project Overview

Gadget Galaxy is a multi-page website built as part of my learning journey in HTML5.

The project showcases different categories of gadgets such as laptops, smartphones, tablets, and more. It focuses primarily on building a **strong foundation in HTML structure and page linking**.

---

##  Objectives

* Learn and implement HTML5 fundamentals
* Understand multi-page website structure
* Practice building a real-world project using only HTML initially
* Gradually enhance the project using CSS3

---

## Technologies Used

HTML5 – Core structure of the website
CSS3 – (Added later for styling and layout)
VS Code – Code editor
Live Server – Real-time preview
Git & GitHub – Version control

---

##  Project Structure

```
Project1/
│── index.html
│── categories.html
│── laptops.html
│── smartphones.html
│── tablets.html
│── smartwatch.html
│── about.html
│── contact.html
│── style.css
│── images/
```

---

##  Features

* Multi-page website with navigation
* Separate pages for different gadget categories
* Laptop brands showcase (Acer, Dell, Apple, Lenovo)
* Clean and structured HTML layout
* Progressive enhancement with CSS

---

## Version History

v1.0 → Initial HTML structure
v1.1 → Multi-page website completed using HTML
v1.2 → Started applying CSS styling

---

##  Note

This project was initially built using only HTML.
At the early stage, I used an AI tool to assist with styling before formally learning CSS.
Currently, I am revisiting and improving the styling based on my own understanding of CSS.


